## Fix: the Rows-per-page selector was hidden along with the footer

Context: surfaced by the browser re-verification of the fix above — the
previous bug had masked it, because the footer never hid. The Rows selector
sat inside the footer, so a single-page result took it down with the page
label and Prev/Next: on the analytics tab (one page of 16 runs) the page size
could never be raised at all, and on the build tab, picking 50 hid the control
that would have put it back to 25.

Changes:

1. `src/front/templates/partials/settings/_settings_runs.html`
   Page label and Prev/Next moved into their own `…PagingControls` wrapper,
   leaving the Rows selector as the footer's own child.
2. `src/front/static/config/js/settings-runs.js`
   `renderPagination()` now toggles two things: the footer follows the table
   (hidden only when there are no rows) and `…PagingControls` hides once the
   result fits one page.
3. `tests/units/front/test_settings_runs_page.py`
   The wrapper exists per tab, the Rows selector renders outside it, and the
   two toggles key off row count and single-page respectively.

