## Fix: the Rows selector flickered on every reload

Context: measured in the browser by stalling `/settings/runs/build` — the
loader's pre-fetch reset still hid the whole footer, so the Rows selector
disappeared for the duration of every fetch and came back when it settled.
Imperceptible against a local registry, visible on a slow one.

Changes:

1. `src/front/static/config/js/settings-runs.js`
   The reset hides only `…PagingControls`, leaving the footer to
   `renderPagination()`, which sets its final state anyway. Both error paths —
   where `renderPagination()` does not run — hide the whole footer, since
   paging a table that is not on screen is meaningless.
2. `tests/units/front/test_settings_runs_page.py`
   The reset does not touch the footer, and each of the two error branches
   hides it.

