## Show the Analytics "Computed in" tile in minutes and seconds

## Context

The KPI tile rendered the raw millisecond count, so a typical Lakeflow run
read as "134210 ms" and left the reader to do the division. The completion
toast had the same problem for the same value.

`task-tracker.js` already owned the app's duration scale (`formatSeconds`),
used by the task tracker and the Runs page, but it was marked "Internal" and
not exported — so the obvious fix was to duplicate the scale. Exporting it
instead keeps one definition, which matters because the same job duration is
visible in both the Analytics tile and the task tracker.

## Changes

1. `src/front/static/global/js/task-tracker.js` — exported the existing
   `formatSeconds` as `window.formatTaskSeconds` and dropped the now-wrong
   "Internal" note from its docstring. No change to the scale itself.
2. `src/front/static/query/js/query-analytics.js` — added `_fmtElapsed(ms)`,
   which converts to seconds and delegates to the shared formatter. Applied
   it to the `aStatElapsed` KPI tile and to the "Analysis done" toast, both
   of which previously concatenated `' ms'`.
3. `tests/units/front/test_analytics_dashboard.py` — added
   `TestElapsedIsHumanReadable` (7 tests). Each was verified to fail when the
   behaviour it pins is reverted, including the ms-to-seconds conversion,
   whose absence would report a 2-minute run as 37 hours.

Resulting scale: `840ms`, `8.3s`, `42.3s`, `1m 14s`, `2m 14s`, `1h 30m`.
Sub-second runs stay in milliseconds rather than rounding to `0.0s`.

